    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.adobe.PremierePro.CC",
      "com.adobe.PremierePro"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://helpx.adobe.com/premiere/desktop/get-started/keyboard-shortcuts/default-keyboard-shortcuts.html",
    "https://helpx.adobe.com/premiere/desktop/get-started/keyboard-shortcuts/about-keyboard-shortcuts.html"
  ],
  "note": "Every row of Adobe's \"Default keyboard shortcuts\" page for Premiere (last updated Jan 7, 2026); helpx.adobe.com/premiere-pro/using/keyboard-shortcuts.html now redirects there. Menu commands carry an empty context, panel commands the panel name. Adobe's macOS column writes \"Delete\" for the backspace key and \"Forward Delete\" for the forward-delete key; those are written here as Backspace and Delete respectively. \"Maximize Frame\" (Window menu) is omitted because the published table prints its key as \"Shift +\" with no key after it. Trailing ellipses in Adobe's command names are dropped. The transport shortcuts kept in `defaults` (J/K/L-style stepping, Space) are not on this page; they are Premiere's long-standing defaults and are retained only as suggested Tune bindings.",
